casa is DevOps tooling for the Discerning Developer: a configuration
management daemon for Unix systems that keeps hosts in a declared
state and keeps them there.

Policy is Lua 5.4. A bundle declares promises for files, packages,
services, users, groups, sysrc and sysctl. Each run converges the host
in a fixed order with per-promise locks, a dry run mode, and a report
that says what was kept, repaired or not. Facts are collected on every
run. Site data lives beside the policy in one declared hierarchy and
is resolved from the point of view of one host.

One binary is the agent, the control plane and the command line.
Three control nodes form a raft cluster that holds policy, membership,
node tags and cluster variables. Agents keep one mTLS connection to a
control node, hear of changes as they commit, fetch policy by content
hash, verify it and converge on a splayed interval. Agents never
listen.
